= Coordination problem — Technical =

Many coordination games contain two or more Nash equilibria. Equilibrium selection can depend on communication, history, salience, conventions, risk dominance, payoff dominance, or learning dynamics. The central obstacle can be incompatible expectations even when interests are broadly aligned.

== Modeling cautions ==
* coordination problem ≠ collective-action problem by identity
* multiple equilibria ≠ conflict of interest
* coordination ≠ centralized control

== References ==
* Thomas C. Schelling, ''The Strategy of Conflict'' (1960).
* David Lewis, ''Convention'' (1969).
* Stanford Encyclopedia of Philosophy, “Game Theory” and “The Free Rider Problem” for the coordination/collective-action distinction.
